    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18506" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fŏlĭātus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		folium, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>leaved</i>, <i>leafy.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caulis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					21, 16, 59, § 99</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">21, 15, 54,
				§ 91</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Pall. Mart. 10 <i>fin.</i></span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arbores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 4, p. 143</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fŏlĭātum</span></b> ,
			i, n. (sc. unguentum), <i>an
				ointment</i> or <i>oil made of the leaves of
				spikenard</i> (hence also called nardinum), <i>nard-oil</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 13, 1, 2, § 15</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Juv.
				6, 465</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 11, 27, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">14, 110, 2</span></i>.</div>
